From: isoriano1968 <isoriano1968@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 19:58:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 38/42] programs: build on AMIX -- dtsession, dtpad, dtstyle,
 dtterm, dtmail, dtcm, dtlogin, ...

Source changes for the AMIX port (__amix__ / AMIXArchitecture next to the
existing platform branches):
- DtWidget Editor.c: wctype.h and wchar.h (wcwidth, putwc/getwc), no
  NO_putwc; DtTerm TermPrimSelect.c: <wctype.h> as on OpenBSD;
- dtstyle ColorFile.c: <fnmatch.h>; dtscreen usleep.c: libc's usleep;
- dtsession SmConMgmt.c, dtcm lexit.c: no nlist()/madvise memory probing,
  as on Linux;
- dtmail: Buffer.hh Chunk declaration, INFTIM, SYSTEM_MAILRC
  (/etc/mail/mailx.rc), signal handler signature, dmx.hh keeps the
  system boolean_t, VendorP.h met with C linkage first (R6.3 has none);
- dtlogin dm.c: <stdarg.h>;
- dtprintinfo: regcmp/regex (NO_REGCOMP) in libUI and PrintObj, the SVR4
  lp spool parser (as on Solaris), <sys/time.h>, boolean after
  <sys/types.h>;
- dtsearchpath UnixEnv.C: rm-based removeFiles and UID/GID_NO_CHANGE as
  on sun, an AMIX MANPATH;
- dtsr Imakefile: depend on libDtSearch.a, not on -lDtSearch;
- util/dttypes: forward declaration for <regexp.h>'s getrnge;
- fontaliases: the linux (X11 font name) aliases for AMIX.
